# These classes are saved to DataStore as JSON by Gson using their *field names* (they have no
# @SerializedName). If R8 ever renamed those fields, data saved by one build would silently fail to
# load in the next, e.g. the wishlist or the background-polling state.
#
# Today app code is outside the R8 scope (see packageScope in app/build.gradle.kts), so nothing here
# is renamed anyway. These rules make that guarantee explicit and keep it if the scope is widened.
# When adding a class that is persisted through Gson without @SerializedName, list it here.

-keepattributes Signature, *Annotation*

-keep class com.example.retrocompanion.data.model.WishlistEntry { *; }
-keep class com.example.retrocompanion.data.model.UnlockStamp { *; }
-keep class com.example.retrocompanion.data.model.AchievementOfTheWeek { *; }
-keep class com.example.retrocompanion.data.polling.PollingState { *; }
-keep class com.example.retrocompanion.data.polling.SeenUnlock { *; }
